* ============================================================
* INDEX X64 CNX SMOKE v1
* ============================================================
* Purpose:
*   CNX-on-x64 (owner ruling 2026-08-09): explicit .cnx on a v64
*   table attaches with an advisory instead of refusing; SET ORDER
*   honors the .cnx (explicit container form AND bare-tag fallback
*   when no .cdx exists); bare REINDEX routes to the CNX engine when
*   the active order is CNX; and the CDX default is UNCHANGED when
*   no .cnx is asked for.
*
* Scope:
*   Non-destructive except a disposable copy in SANDBOX.
*   Self-bootstrapping; erases its own copy at both ends.
*
* Guard rationale:
*   CNX was re-enacted to x64 standards (ramfs/vdisk in-RAM indexing,
*   XIDX-TXN-02 M1 realtime maintenance); the old blanket refusal in
*   SET INDEX / SET ORDER was stale policy. LMDB-backed CDX remains
*   the preferred and default x64 index.
* ============================================================

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO INDEX X64 CNX SMOKE v1
ECHO ============================================================

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/SANDBOX
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/SANDBOX
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE students_cnx64_smoke CONFIRM

ECHO
ECHO --- GUARD 1: CDX DEFAULT UNCHANGED (no explicit .cnx anywhere) ---
USE students
AREA
* Expect: auto-attached CDX order (students.cdx); flavor v64.

ECHO
ECHO --- MAKE DISPOSABLE X64 COPY (no .cdx sidecar rides along) ---
COPY TO students_cnx64_smoke
CLOSE
USE students_cnx64_smoke
AREA
COUNT

ECHO
ECHO --- BUILD A CNX FOR THE X64 COPY ---
CNX CREATE
CNX ADDTAG SID
CNX ADDTAG LNAME
REBUILD
* REBUILD is the CNX engine; it carries no flavor guard and must
* populate both tags on this v64 table.

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE A: EXPLICIT .cnx ATTACH (advisory, NOT refusal) ---
SET INDEX TO students_cnx64_smoke.cnx
* Expect: "advisory -- LMDB-backed CDX is the preferred index" then
* "SET INDEX: CNX attached". The old output was a hard refusal:
* "True x64/v128 tables require CDX (LMDB-backed)."

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE C1: EXPLICIT CONTAINER + TAG ORDER ---
SETORDER students_cnx64_smoke.cnx LNAME
AREA
TOP
TUPLE SID,LNAME,FNAME
SKIP 1
TUPLE SID,LNAME,FNAME
* Expect: LNAME-ordered traversal under the CNX (not physical order).

ECHO
ECHO --- SEEK UNDER CNX ORDER ---
SEEK "White"
TUPLE SID,LNAME,FNAME

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE D2: BARE REINDEX ROUTES TO CNX (active CNX order) ---
REINDEX
* Expect: "REINDEX default -> CNX (active CNX order, via REBUILD)".
* The old behavior forced CDX/BUILDLMDB and failed on the missing env.

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE C2: BARE-TAG FALLBACK FINDS THE .cnx (fresh session) ---
WORKSPACE CLOSE
USE students_cnx64_smoke
SET ORDER TO SID
AREA
TOP
TUPLE SID,LNAME,FNAME
* Expect: advisory "no .cdx container found; using existing CNX",
* then SID-ordered traversal. The old behavior failed with
* "file not found: ...students_cnx64_smoke.cdx".

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE B: WORKSPACE OPEN DBF CNX (explicit index source) ---
WORKSPACE CLOSE
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF CNX
SELECT STUDENTS_CNX64_SMOKE
AREA
* Expect: under explicit CNX mode the x64 copy attaches its .cnx, while
* plain students (no .cnx present) opens WITHOUT an attached index --
* the requested mode is honored, not silently swapped to CDX. This is a
* verification phase: the WORKSPACE mode plumbing predates AIF-099 and
* carries no flavor guard; this proves it on an x64 table.

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE E: CROSS-SLOT DECOY (owner-caught leak, 2026-08-09) ---
* The old dirs_for_mode searched the INDEXES_X32 slot BEFORE the configured
* INDEXES slot whenever CNX was wanted, so an x64 table could attach a
* same-stem .cnx built over a DIFFERENT table (observed live:
* dbf/x64/STUDENTS.dbf wearing indexes/x32/STUDENTS.cnx). Plant a decoy
* copy of the smoke's .cnx in a dir posing as the x32 slot; the attach
* MUST come from the configured slot (INDEXES/SANDBOX), not the decoy.
COPY FILE INDEXES\SANDBOX\students_cnx64_smoke.cnx TO tmp\students_cnx64_smoke.cnx OVERWRITE
SET PATH INDEXES_X32 tmp
WORKSPACE CLOSE
WORKSPACE OPEN DBF CNX
SELECT STUDENTS_CNX64_SMOKE
AREA
* Expect: Index file path contains INDEXES\SANDBOX (configured slot), NOT
* \tmp\ (the decoy posing as the x32 slot). Under the pre-fix order the
* decoy would win and AREA would show the tmp path -- the known-bad that
* the single-slot SANDBOX environment could not previously express.
SET PATH INDEXES_X32 INDEXES/x32

ECHO
ECHO --- SCOPE F: ATTACHED CNX WINS BARE-TAG SET ORDER (no CDX hop) ---
* Give the DISPOSABLE COPY both containers so the hop is expressible
* self-contained (v1 of this phase used SANDBOX students.cnx -- a file that
* only ever "existed" as the pre-fix x32-slot leak masquerading as local;
* the phase was designed on evidence planted by the bug under test).
* With BOTH containers present and the CNX deliberately attached, bare
* SET ORDER TO <tag> must resolve on the ATTACHED CNX -- pre-fix it hopped
* to the .cdx (observed live 2026-08-09: REINDEX honored the CNX while
* SET ORDER TO TAG switched to CDX).
WORKSPACE CLOSE
USE students_cnx64_smoke
CDX CREATE
CDX ADDTAG SID
BUILDLMDB
SET INDEX TO students_cnx64_smoke.cnx
SET ORDER TO SID
AREA
* Expect: advisory then "SET INDEX: CNX attached"; then
* "SET ORDER: CNX TAG 'SID'" with Index file ...students_cnx64_smoke.cnx --
* NOT "CDX TAG" / .cdx. Both containers are erased with the copy at cleanup.

ECHO
ECHO --- CLEANUP ---
WORKSPACE CLOSE
ERASE students_cnx64_smoke CONFIRM
* Note: the decoy tmp\students_cnx64_smoke.cnx remains in TMP (transient dir).

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO INDEX X64 CNX SMOKE v1 DONE
ECHO ============================================================
